+# SMS authentication integration
+
+This repository is a static homepage. `auth.js` expects same-origin authentication endpoints; until they are implemented, requests fail with a visible error and the page does not claim to send a text or authenticate a customer.
+
+## Send a code
+
+`POST /api/auth/send-code`
+
+Request: `{ "phone": "+15551234567", "purpose": "rewards" }` (or `"order"`).
+
+Successful JSON response: `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-generated-id" }`.
+
+Generate a cryptographically random six-digit code on the server, expire it after five minutes, and send it through your SMS provider. Bind the challenge to the phone, purpose, and initiating session. Apply phone/session/IP rate limits and attempt limits. Resending must invalidate the previous code. Do not return the code to the client or log it.
+
+For WebOTP and supported platform autofill, send a domain-bound message over HTTPS. The last line must contain the production hostname and code, for example:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 123456. It expires in 5 minutes.
+
+@your-production-hostname.com #123456
+```
+
+Replace the example hostname with the actual page hostname. The browser controls SMS consent and availability; customers can always type or paste the code. The client uses one labeled text field with `inputmode="numeric"` and `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, and progressively enhances it with WebOTP when available.
+
+## Verify a code
+
+`POST /api/auth/verify-code`
+
+Request: `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-generated-id", "code": "123456", "purpose": "rewards" }`.
+
+Only return `{ "verified": true }` after server verification. Consume the challenge atomically, establish a session with a Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookie, and enforce expiry and attempt limits. The client then navigates to `/rewards` or `/order-online`; these routes must enforce authentication independently. Return a non-2xx response for invalid/expired codes and HTTP 429 for rate limits. Authentication responses should use `Cache-Control: no-store`. Apply same-origin/CSRF checks to both endpoints.
+
+The phone field currently supports US numbers (+1). Extend country selection and server-side normalization together if other markets are needed.
+
+Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp
